WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.109 --> 00:00:02.720
(guitar strumming)

00:00:02.720 --> 00:00:04.460
(distant applause)

00:00:04.460 --> 00:00:05.670
- I think there's something about

00:00:05.670 --> 00:00:07.507
the more difficult it
is to get to a place,

00:00:07.507 --> 00:00:10.454
it seems like it's more
valuable when you're there.

00:00:10.454 --> 00:00:12.704
(chanting)

00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:15.780
As a photographer, my end goal really is

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:17.790
to make people see the landscape

00:00:17.790 --> 00:00:20.130
in a completely new perspective.

00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:22.423
It's about showing things
in a different light.

00:00:35.762 --> 00:00:38.304
I don't really see
myself as a photographer.

00:00:38.304 --> 00:00:42.893
Um, I see myself as an artist
working with photography.

00:00:44.030 --> 00:00:46.320
Well, I've always been pretty
obsessed with mountains.

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:48.920
Rock formations and pinnacles
and that kind of thing.

00:00:48.920 --> 00:00:51.700
Growing up in Liverpool,
glaciers were always something

00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:54.660
that I had never really
had that much access to.

00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:56.740
When I was approached by Coors Light,

00:00:56.740 --> 00:00:58.380
to shoot in an incredible place like this,

00:00:58.380 --> 00:01:00.000
I thought it was a really great chance

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:02.590
to show something which
wasn't seen before.

00:01:02.590 --> 00:01:05.340
The color of the ice underneath
the light of the drone.

00:01:06.290 --> 00:01:08.790
Tomorrow, if we can go into Pastoruri

00:01:08.790 --> 00:01:11.350
in order to get to a
really good viewpoint,

00:01:11.350 --> 00:01:12.230
we have to hike.

00:01:15.050 --> 00:01:17.944
New experiences are crucial for me.

00:01:17.944 --> 00:01:20.853
I just explore and see where it takes me.

00:01:23.340 --> 00:01:24.173
Wow.

00:01:25.170 --> 00:01:27.613
The scale of this place
is just incredible.

00:01:32.022 --> 00:01:33.773
- Probably, like, it's gonna get tougher

00:01:33.773 --> 00:01:35.690
on this walk.

00:01:35.690 --> 00:01:38.910
- Yeah, I know it gets steep somewhere.

00:01:38.910 --> 00:01:40.500
I don't mind going a little bit higher.

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:42.510
I think there's more to discover.

00:01:42.510 --> 00:01:44.200
Tonight, I do wanna come away

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:47.613
with compositions which
are quite a bit different.

00:01:47.613 --> 00:01:50.363
(exciting music)

00:01:58.883 --> 00:02:01.580
(flute)

00:02:01.580 --> 00:02:03.220
When the full moon comes up,

00:02:03.220 --> 00:02:05.740
everything is gonna be bathed in light.

00:02:05.740 --> 00:02:09.100
So, I think it will be a
good idea to start shooting,

00:02:09.100 --> 00:02:10.053
like, now-ish.

00:02:20.763 --> 00:02:22.550
One of the things about
exploring a landscape

00:02:22.550 --> 00:02:24.500
for me is being able to shoot at night.

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:31.060
I've been using drones with
lights attached to them

00:02:31.060 --> 00:02:34.540
and that allows me to
illuminate the landscape

00:02:34.540 --> 00:02:36.263
as you would in a studio.

00:02:38.150 --> 00:02:40.750
That was kind of the challenge,
trying to see in the dark.

00:02:40.750 --> 00:02:43.050
Everything is more
difficult at this altitude.

00:02:45.552 --> 00:02:49.420
(distant) No, no, no, no.

00:02:49.420 --> 00:02:53.053
That shoot was kinda low
and it kind of landed badly.

00:02:54.980 --> 00:02:56.950
It's mainly this.

00:02:56.950 --> 00:02:59.820
I started losing fingers
in my index finger

00:02:59.820 --> 00:03:02.347
and middle finger.

00:03:02.347 --> 00:03:03.180
(laugh)

00:03:03.180 --> 00:03:04.930
I can't even speak properly
’cause it's so cold.

00:03:04.930 --> 00:03:06.963
I’d like to test this again
just to see if it works.

00:03:08.707 --> 00:03:11.457
(haunting music)

00:03:16.260 --> 00:03:18.870
With this project, I
was seeking to produce

00:03:18.870 --> 00:03:20.690
a series of images that tells a story

00:03:20.690 --> 00:03:25.093
of this place and express
my own ideas of exploration.

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:31.420
I don't think I'll ever stop exploring.

00:03:31.420 --> 00:03:32.870
That's what it comes down to.

00:03:34.310 --> 00:03:36.160
Going out of your comfort zone.

00:03:36.160 --> 00:03:39.133
You know, each time you do something,
just push a little bit further.

